# a PSRAM read restarts its data phase while start is high: CS1/CS2 low without bound -> MT1
sed qspi_ctrl.v s/^\( *\)if (late [&][&] !t_we)$/\1if (start [&][&] psram [&][&] !t_we) cnt <= 3'd7; else if (late [&][&] !t_we)/
# CS is high for one clock between transactions (the next CS falls in the S_END cycle) -> MT2
sed qspi_ctrl.v s/^\( *\)sck   <= 1'b0;$/\1sck   <= 1'b0; if (!init [&][&] start) cs_n <= ~sel_now;/
